    return "---\nid: rust-symbol-analysis\ntype: spec\ntitle: \"Rust Symbol Analysis\"\nversion: 1\nspec_type: algorithm\ncreated_at: 2026-02-06T07:54:55.631856+00:00\nupdated_at: 2026-02-06T07:54:55.631856+00:00\nrequirements:\n  total: 7\n  ids:\n    - R1\n    - R2\n    - R3\n    - R4\n    - R5\n    - R6\n    - R7\ndesign_elements:\n  has_mermaid: true\n  has_json_schema: false\n  has_pseudo_code: false\n  has_api_spec: false\n  has_semantic_diagrams: false\n  diagrams:\n    - type: flowchart\n      title: \"Rust Symbol Extraction Flow\"\nhistory:\n  - timestamp: 2026-02-06T07:54:55.631856+00:00\n    agent: \"mcp\"\n    tool: \"create_spec\"\n    action: \"created\"\n  - timestamp: 2026-02-06T07:55:17.128879+00:00\n    agent: \"gemini:pro\"\n    tool: \"create_spec\"\n    action: \"created\"\n  - timestamp: 2026-02-06T07:55:47.580722+00:00\n    agent: \"codex:max\"\n    tool: \"review_spec\"\n    action: \"reviewed\"\ncapability_refs:\n  - id: existing-project-standardization\n    role: primary\n    gap: managed-and-semantic-production-gates\n    claim: managed-and-semantic-production-gates\n    coverage: full\n    rationale: \"Rust symbol analysis supports semantic coverage and brownfield source understanding during standardization.\"\n---\n\n<spec>\n\n# Rust Symbol Analysis\n\n## Overview\n<!-- type: doc lang: markdown -->\n\nThis spec defines the algorithm and data mapping for extracting semantic symbols from Rust source code within the Lens analysis engine. It extends the existing `SymbolTableBuilder` to support Rust AST nodes (generated by tree-sitter-rust), mapping them to the unified `Symbol` and `TypeInfo` structures. This enables cross-language analysis features like \"Go to Definition\" and \"Find References\" for Rust files.\n\n## Requirements\n<!-- type: doc lang: markdown -->\n\n### R1 - Extract Rust Functions\n\n```yaml\nid: R1\npriority: high\nstatus: draft\n```\n\nThe system must extract function definitions (`fn_item`), including name, return type, parameters, and visibility modifiers.\n\n### R2 - Extract Rust Structs\n\n```yaml\nid: R2\npriority: high\nstatus: draft\n```\n\nThe system must extract struct definitions (`struct_item`), including name and fields (named or tuple).\n\n### R3 - Extract Rust Traits\n\n```yaml\nid: R3\npriority: medium\nstatus: draft\n```\n\nThe system must extract trait definitions (`trait_item`), including name and associated items.\n\n### R4 - Extract Rust Impls\n\n```yaml\nid: R4\npriority: medium\nstatus: draft\n```\n\nThe system must extract implementation blocks (`impl_item`), linking methods to the implemented type or trait.\n\n### R5 - Extract Rust Constants\n\n```yaml\nid: R5\npriority: low\nstatus: draft\n```\n\nThe system must extract constants (`const_item`) and static variables (`static_item`).\n\n### R6 - Extract Rust Doc Comments\n\n```yaml\nid: R6\npriority: medium\nstatus: draft\n```\n\nThe system must extract documentation comments, handling both outer (`///`) and inner (`//!`) doc styles.\n\n### R7 - Parse Rust Types\n\n```yaml\nid: R7\npriority: medium\nstatus: draft\n```\n\nThe system must parse Rust type signatures (e.g., `Option<String>`, `Vec<i32>`, `&str`) into the unified `TypeInfo` structure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n<!-- type: doc lang: markdown -->\n\n### Scenario: Happy Path - Struct and Impl\n\n- **GIVEN** A Rust file with a struct and an impl block\n- **WHEN** The file is parsed and `build_rust` is called\n- **THEN** The symbol table should contain symbols for `MyStruct`, `new`, and `process`, with `new` and `process` scoped under the impl/struct.\n\n### Scenario: Function with Generics\n\n- **GIVEN** A Rust function with generic parameters and a complex return type\n- **WHEN** The function is analyzed\n- **THEN** The symbol table should contain a function symbol with `TypeInfo` reflecting `fn(T) -> Option<T>`.\n\n### Scenario: Doc Comments\n\n- **GIVEN** A Rust file with `///` doc comments above a function\n- **WHEN** The file is analyzed\n- **THEN** The symbol for the function should have the doc field populated with the comment text.\n\n## Diagrams\n<!-- type: doc lang: markdown -->\n\n### Rust Symbol Extraction Flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n    Start((Start build_rust))\n    VisitRoot[Visit Root Node]\n    CheckKind{Node Kind?} \n    VisitFn[[visit_rust_function]]\n    VisitStruct[[visit_rust_struct]]\n    VisitTrait[[visit_rust_trait]]\n    VisitImpl[[visit_rust_impl]]\n    VisitConst[[visit_rust_const]]\n    VisitMod[[visit_rust_mod]]\n    Recurse[[Recurse Children]]\n    ExtractFnInfo[Extract Name, Type, Doc]\n    AddFnSym[Add Function Symbol]\n    PushFnScope[Push Scope]\n    VisitFnBody[[Visit Params & Body]]\n    PopFnScope[Pop Scope]\n    ExtractStructInfo[Extract Name, Doc]\n    AddStructSym[Add Struct Symbol]\n    PushStructScope[Push Scope]\n    VisitStructFields[[Visit Fields]]\n    PopStructScope[Pop Scope]\n    ExtractImplInfo[Extract Type/Trait Name]\n    AddImplSym[Add Impl Symbol]\n    PushImplScope[Push Scope]\n    VisitImplBody[[Visit Methods]]\n    PopImplScope[Pop Scope]\n    Start -->|| VisitRoot\n    VisitRoot -->|| CheckKind\n    CheckKind -->|function_item| VisitFn\n    CheckKind -->|struct_item| VisitStruct\n    CheckKind -->|trait_item| VisitTrait\n    CheckKind -->|impl_item| VisitImpl\n    CheckKind -->|const/static_item| VisitConst\n    CheckKind -->|mod_item| VisitMod\n    CheckKind -->|other| Recurse\n    VisitFn -->|| ExtractFnInfo\n    ExtractFnInfo -->|| AddFnSym\n    AddFnSym -->|| PushFnScope\n    PushFnScope -->|| VisitFnBody\n    VisitFnBody -->|| PopFnScope\n    VisitStruct -->|| ExtractStructInfo\n    ExtractStructInfo -->|| AddStructSym\n    AddStructSym -->|| PushStructScope\n    PushStructScope -->|| VisitStructFields\n    VisitStructFields -->|| PopStructScope\n```\n\n</spec>\n"
